{
  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only (config_001, scgpt+transformer) achieves the best accuracy (0.514) at very low cost (0.51 GPU hrs), while the best multimodal config (config_009, scgpt+imagenet_vit_l+transformer+concat) is slightly behind at 0.507. The resnet50 image encoder (config_012, 0.471) is clearly worse. This suggests the imagenet_vit_l + scgpt + transformer backbone is the strongest multimodal combination, but the concat fusion may be preventing the image modality from contributing positively. Question: Does weighted fusion allow the model to better balance RNA and image contributions, potentially closing or exceeding the RNA-only gap? config_039 is the single-variable extension of config_009 (only fusion changes from concat to weighted), making it the cleanest test of whether fusion strategy is the bottleneck. Why this experiment: It directly exploits the strongest multimodal evidence while testing the one unexplored design axis on that backbone. If it pushes accuracy above 0.514, it validates a multimodal path; if not, it narrows the search toward RNA-only or simpler aggregations. Expected cost is similar to config_009 (~4 GPU hrs) since the architecture is identical, only the fusion weighting differs."
}

